# Copy to ~/.mbsyncrc and fill in the placeholders.
# App-specific password from https://app.fastmail.com/settings/security/devicekeys

IMAPAccount fastmail
Host          imap.fastmail.com
Port          993
User          you@fastmail.com
PassCmd       "security find-generic-password -a you@fastmail.com -s mbsync -w"
TLSType       IMAPS
TLSVersions   +1.2 +1.3
AuthMechs     LOGIN

IMAPStore fastmail-remote
Account fastmail

MaildirStore fastmail-local
Subfolders Verbatim
Path       ~/Mail/Fastmail/
Inbox      ~/Mail/Fastmail/INBOX

Channel fastmail
Far     :fastmail-remote:
Near    :fastmail-local:
# Which IMAP folders to mirror. Fastmail "labels" are exposed as IMAP folders,
# so this is the knob for filtering them. Examples:
#   Patterns *                    sync everything
#   Patterns INBOX                inbox only — archived/labelled mail won't sync
#   Patterns INBOX INBOX/*        inbox plus its sub-folders
#   Patterns * !Archive !Trash    everything except the named folders
#
# The default below syncs everything EXCEPT the spam folder, under the names
# the common providers give it. Anyone can put mail in your spam folder, and
# whatever syncs is parsed, indexed, OCR'd and returned by search alongside
# your real mail, so leaving it out is the safer starting point. Folders are
# matched by name only: if your provider calls its spam folder something else,
# add it here. A name with a space needs the quotes, with the ! inside them.
# To index spam anyway, replace the line with `Patterns *`. Trash is synced;
# add !Trash (Gmail: "![Gmail]/Trash") to leave deleted mail out as well.
Patterns * !Spam !Junk "!Junk Mail" "!Junk E-mail" "!Bulk Mail" "![Gmail]/Spam"
Create  Near
SyncState *
# Read-only sync: changes in Fastmail flow down, never up.
Sync    Pull
Expunge Near
# Example Cap each folder to the 6000 newest messages. mbsync has no date-range
# filter; this is the closest knob and works well if you don't want to
# pull years of archive on first sync. Remove the line to sync everything.
#MaxMessages 6000
